  <note>
    <content>
      <p>RK25 used the frozen RK20 train, development, test and sequence-OOD partitions with 4,019, 503, 490 and 1,336 constructs. The Boël author multiclass model was refit from scratch using train only: 61 single-codon slopes came from train E0/E5 and the final multinomial logistic model used all train rows with fixed L2 = 0.01. No RK24 fitted coefficients or Boël Published coefficients were used. Four frozen ribokinetic_all seeds and frozen ridge_all and HistGB predictions were aligned without new neural or generator training.</p>
      <p>On sequence-OOD, all-channel minus author Spearman is minus 0.21811836219540887 with 95% hierarchical-bootstrap interval minus 0.2722711773243162 to minus 0.16334044169079254. All-channel minus author cluster-balanced MSE is plus 0.7306069546160505 with interval 0.5341382109633555 to 0.9258797959656737. Both mechanism endpoints fail. Author minus ridge_all Spearman is plus 0.20952136656831705 with interval 0.15881562830926724 to 0.2602926941378022, and cluster-MSE is minus 0.8290870762002958 with interval minus 1.004941052200879 to minus 0.6532704006471712. Author minus HistGB Spearman is plus 0.2080114740266785 with interval 0.15728926553841197 to 0.25857330923095795, and cluster-MSE is minus 0.7047199149791634 with interval minus 0.8672243031203977 to minus 0.5434487638967203. Both author-reference comparisons pass two of two endpoints.</p>
      <p>The estimand is the mean of four per-seed effects, not a prediction ensemble. Inference used 20,000 hierarchical bootstrap replicates with seed 20261125, resampling operational protein clusters and training seeds. All six empirical sign-tail and Holm-adjusted p values are zero because no opposite-sign tail occurred; this does not rescue the two mechanism endpoints, whose point and interval directions fail. Development showed the same ordering. Test was descriptive only and was not included in the six-endpoint Holm family.</p>
      <p>Independent OOD acceptance passed 678 of 678 checks; development acceptance separately passed 337 of 337. Maximum prediction difference is 1.021405182655144e-14, maximum metric difference is 4.440892098500626e-16, maximum bootstrap-array difference is 1.7763568394002505e-15 and maximum inference difference is 4.440892098500626e-16. The independent verifier reproduced all three Gate decisions. The earlier gzip CSV replay difference of 8.881784197001252e-16 was handled by the frozen 1e-12 numerical tolerance while identities, labels, clusters and seeds remained strict; the failed first attempt did not compute test or OOD metrics and was not used as scientific evidence.</p>
      <p>The supported conclusion is limited to this reused cross-protein, non-synonymous sequence-OOD benchmark. The author model is stronger than ridge_all and HistGB, but all-channel does not beat the author model. The strong comparator chain fails, RK-G1 remains false and expensive generator training remains unauthorized. This is not fixed-protein synonymous causality, translation velocity, mRNA decay, full spatial coupling, functional-untouched confirmation, CodonFlow-RK superiority, external SOTA or generative quality. Functional untouched data were not accessed. Frozen evidence commit 44014ad0fc923fba65d52fcda953117d9c822051; scientific closeout commit 38ecaf7a222f5ce74ceba16f29f3043071bf5d9e.</p>
    </content>
